; expect 42
; The AXTAG scan's frame count must not grow with the source size.
;
; `scanAxtagsFrom` walked the source one byte per recursive call. Three
; of its four branches were plain self tail calls, which cost nothing
; under a compiler that eliminates them - and stage1 does not eliminate
; them here, so a stage1-built binary that has not been through `opt`
; paid one frame per ordinary byte of every module it resolved.
;
; It was invisible for as long as no module was big enough to reach the
; limit, and it was reached by ordinary growth: adding to
; `self_host/codegen.ax` pushed the FORMATTED copy of it from 215,369
; to 221,940 bytes, and `check-fmt.sh` - which re-runs the suites
; against a formatted copy of the whole repository, the largest input
; anything here compiles - segfaulted on `300-pipeline`. Nothing about
; that change touched the lexer.
;
; Measured on the pre-fix spelling: 400 KB of comment-free source
; segfaults, while 400 KB that is almost entirely comment lines does
; not - because a comment is skipped in one step and an ordinary byte
; costs a frame. That asymmetry is why `840-large-lex.ax` did not catch
; this: it exercises `lex`, and nothing exercised `scanAxtags` at
; scale.
;
; 26 bytes doubled fourteen times is ~426 KB, comfortably past where
; the recursive spelling died, and one line in two is an AXTAG so the
; scan has real work to do rather than one long skip. Restoring the
; recursive spelling fails this case with SIGSEGV.
(import Str)
(import Vec)
(import lexer)

(:: rep (-> String Int String))
(fn (rep s n)
  (if (== n 0) s (rep (strConcat s s) (- n 1))))

(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (let ((src (rep ";@axiom:pure\n(fn (f x) x)\n" 14)))
    (if (&& (> (strLen src) 400000)
            (== (vecLen (scanAxtags src)) 16384))
        42
        1)))
